tance coverage [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]are present.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]2[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]finish_usage_limit_auto_disable.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/finish_usage_limit_auto_disable.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim] Parent: [#87AFFF][/dim]202608/llm_usage_limit_auto_disable.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-n4.5[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-n4/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]sase-n4.5.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make first usage-limit disable atomic in sase-core[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]atomic-disable[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]atomic-disable: add a Rust-core and Python-binding operation that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]atomically writes a provider disable only when no active record exists, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]returns whether this caller won the window, preserves the existing [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]unconditional manual replacement APIs, and proves first-writer behavior [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]under real contention.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Correct matching, provider attribution, and end-to-end [/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]behavior[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]runtime-correctness[dim] · [dim][/dim]after atomic-disable[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]runtime-correctness: consume the atomic store result in usage-limit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]enforcement, make replace_patterns literal even for an empty list, keep [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]retry attribution pinned to the execution provider recorded for each [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]attempt including fallback attempts, and add a full fakey [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]invocation-to-disable-to-notification acceptance test that proves one [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]attempt, unchanged error propagation, and no collateral provider [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]disable.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Restore disable provenance and document usage-limit policy[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]surface-and-document[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]surface-and-document: render automatic, manual, and unknown disable [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]provenance in the current split Launch Control provider modules and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]top-bar tooltip, add the commented usage_limit configuration block [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]without disturbing newer config fields, document detection, reset hints,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]machine-wide expiry, clearing, retry precedence, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]extension/replacement semantics, and cover the surfaces including [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]intentional visual snapshots.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-n4.5","llm_provider":"grok","model":"grok-4.6","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-n4.5.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-8fa5da8d80dca530f92deb5c8d431b53","started_at":"2026-08-16T18:22:54.515698+00:00","state":"active"},{"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"9667eeea7c5846009defee34a65dce61081784bee744c0906b4fc91b42efb016","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-n4.4/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"meta":{"digest":"2cdfac5889977148d57ebadaf02354a6a20ac2ae7359b561f18ebe7f93b5bad1","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-n4.4/meta.json","size_bytes":370},"state":{"digest":"d92c51e031ce693b50ed042411c9500ed8785e4c734200fa3d30c5f548b08b7b","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-n4.4/state.json",